      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 149,
      "outputTokens": 1101,
      "costUsd": 0.0099835,
      "pronunciationText": "In a geometric sequence, each term is the one before, multiplied by the same number. That number is called the common ratio, r. So a sub n equals r times ay sub n minus one. To test a sequence, divide each term by the one before it. Take two, six, eighteen, fifty-four. Six over two is three, eighteen over six is three, and fifty-four over eighteen is three. Every ratio is the same, so it's geometric, with r equal to three. Now try five, ten, twenty, thirty-five. The first two ratios are two, but thirty-five over twenty is one and three quarters. One different ratio is enough. It's not geometric."
    },
