      "inputTokens": 109,
      "outputTokens": 774,
      "costUsd": 0.0070205,
      "pronunciationText": "The ratio doesn't have to be a whole number. One hundred, fifty, twenty-five, twelve and a half has r equal to a half. Each term is half the last, so the terms shrink towards zero. One, minus two, four, minus eight has r equal to minus two. Multiplying by a negative number flips the sign every time, so the terms alternate. But r can never be zero. If it were, every term after the first would be zero, and the ratio test would divide by zero."
