      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 156,
      "outputTokens": 1142,
      "costUsd": 0.010356,
      "pronunciationText": "Now a formula for any term. Start with a, the first term. The second term is a times r. The third is a times r times r, which is a r squared. Each step along multiplies by r once more. Just like arithmetic sequences, the nth term is n minus one steps from the first. So a sub n equals a, times r to the power n minus one. Back to the paper. The unfolded sheet is the first term, a tenth of a millimetre. After forty-two folds, it's the forty-third term, a tenth of a millimetre times two to the forty-two. Two to the forty-two is more than four trillion. That's why it reaches about four hundred and forty thousand kilometres."
    },
