      "outputTokens": 1059,
      "costUsd": 0.009604,
      "pronunciationText": "Which term is the first to go over one thousand? Set three times two to the n minus one above one thousand. Divide by three, so two to the n minus one is more than one thousand over three. To get n out of the power, take logs of both sides, and divide by log two. Log two is positive, so the inequality stays the same way round. Then n minus one is more than about eight point three eight, so n is more than nine point three eight. Positions are whole numbers, so it's the tenth term. Check both sides. The ninth term is seven hundred and sixty-eight, below one thousand, and the tenth is one thousand five hundred and thirty-six."
