      "costUsd": 0.0096305,
      "pronunciationText": "What if you're given two terms, but not the first? The third term is twelve, and the sixth term is ninety-six. From the third term to the sixth is three multiplications, so ninety-six is twelve times r cubed. Dividing cancels a. So r cubed is eight, and r is two. Then a times r squared is twelve, so a times four is twelve, and ay is three. Here the gap is three steps, an odd number, so there's only one real cube root. With an even number of steps and a positive result, r could be positive or negative, so you'd get two possible sequences. A negative result would give no real r at all."
    },
