      "pronunciationText": "First, r is minus twelve over four, which is minus three. The sixth term is five multiplications from the first, so it's four times minus three to the power five. An odd power of a negative number is negative, so the answer is minus nine hundred and seventy-two. Two thousand nine hundred and sixteen is wrong. It uses the power six, one multiplication too many."
