      "pronunciationText": "From the second term to the fourth is two multiplications, so fifty-four is six times r squared. So r squared is nine, and r is three or minus three. Then ay is six over r. So ay is two with r equal to three, or ay is minus two with r equal to minus three. Giving only r equals three is wrong. It misses the second sequence: minus two, six, minus eighteen, fifty-four."
