      "costUsd": 0.0071400000000000005,
      "pronunciationText": "So a geometric sequence multiplies by the same ratio every step, and its nth term is a times r to the n minus one. But what happens when we add the terms? Put one grain of rice on the first square of a chessboard, two on the second, four on the third, doubling each time. The running totals are one, three, seven, fifteen and thirty-one. How many grains are on the first ten squares, without adding them one by one?"
